  "question": {
    "text": "A tiny spherical oil drop carrying a net charge <math><mi>q</mi></math> is balanced in still air with vertical uniform electric field of strength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>81</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>When the field is switched off, the drop is observed to fall with terminal velocity<math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> Given <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> viscosity of the air =<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi></math>and the density of oil&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>900</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>kg</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> the magnitude of <math><mi>q</mi></math> is"
  },
